/*
:name: concat_literal_lane
:type: error
:error: no declared bit width
:help: bind it to a typed name first
*/

// Same rule, reached the other way: a literal written DIRECTLY as a lane has no
// declared type either, however it is spelled. The fix is to bind it to a typed
// name first (`const one:u8 = 1`), which states the window explicitly.
comb concat_literal_lane(a:u4) -> (z:u12) {
  z = concat(a, 0ub01)
}
